<title>JAPAN: Kawasaki Steel unit in ferroalloy venture.</title>
<headline>Kawasaki Steel unit in ferroalloy venture.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Kawasaki Steel Corp subsidiary said on Friday it reached a basic agreement with a unit of Associated Manganese Mines of South Africa Ltd (Assmang) on a joint venture to produce 30,000 tonnes of medium- and low-carbon ferromanganese per year.</p>
<p>The $20 million project, to be located in South Africa, is expected to begin production in early 1998.</p>
<p>The venture will be 50 percent-owned by Assmang subsidiary Feralloys Ltd and 40 percent-owned by Kawasaki unit Mizushima Ferroalloy Co. The remaining 10 percent will be held by Sumitomo Corp.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
